Expand around each center; count each successful expansion as one palindromic substring.

```python
def count_palindromes(s):
    count = 0
    for i in range(len(s)):
        for lo, hi in ((i, i), (i, i + 1)):
            while lo >= 0 and hi < len(s) and s[lo] == s[hi]:
                count += 1
                lo -= 1
                hi += 1
    return count
```

